    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense from a sociological perspective, but some critics argue that those systemic factors don't fully explain everything. They point to differences in family structure, cultural emphasis on certain types of learning, or even inherent cognitive differences as contributing factors. How would an objective researcher weigh those more \"internal\" or cultural explanations against the systemic ones?",
